## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of per-tenant routing, docker configs, and zero-downtime reconfiguration in a multi-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Traefik dynamic config and weighted routing
- Docker Configs for per-tenant policy
- TLS termination at edge proxy
- Multi-DC docker-dca deployment basics
- Observability of per-tenant routing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Traefik dynamic config snippet (example)
{
  "http": {
    "routers": {
      "tenant-ab": {
        "rule": "Host(`api.local`)",
        "tls": { "certResolver": "myresolver" },
        "service": "ab-backend"
      }
    },
    "services": {
      "ab-backend": {
        "loadBalancer": {
          "weighted": {
            "services": [
              { "name": "api-v1", "weight": 80 },
              { "name": "api-v2", "weight": 20 }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant weight changes in production?
- How would you handle missing or malformed ab-split entries?
- How would you monitor skew and rollback strategies?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a tenant-aware resilience and security workflow across DCs, combining secret management, mTLS, and controlled fault injection.

## Key Concepts
- Vault-driven per-tenant fault policies
- Nginx Lua for ingress-level fault injection
- SPIFFE SVIDs and TLS rotation per workload
- SLA-based canary/rollback and observability

## Code Example
```javascript
function getTenantPolicy(tenant) {
  // pseudo-call to Vault to fetch policy
  return vault.fetchPolicy(tenant) || { latencyMs: 0, dropRate: 0 };
}
function shouldInject(tenant) {
  const p = getTenantPolicy(tenant);
  return Math.random() < p.dropRate ? 'drop' : 'latency';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test SLA breach detection and rollback in a live cluster?
- How do you ensure policy changes are hot-applied without restarting proxies?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-DC data residency controls, real-time policy updates, and secure audit logging in a docker-dca setup.

## Key Concepts
- Data residency and cross-DC egress policies
- WASM-based per-tenant policy engine (Wasmtime)
- Vault-driven tenant configs and SPIFFE SVID rotation
- SIEM-based auditing and reproducible bootstrap

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo policy evaluation sketch
function evaluate(event, tenant) {
  if (event.destDC === 'DC-B' && !tenant.optIn) return 'block';
  redact(event.payload, tenant.schema);
  return 'allow';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify policy correctness across DC failover?
- How would you handle policy module hot-reload and versioning?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end trust from image provenance to runtime policy enforcement, plus canary control and rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Content Trust/Notary for image provenance
- SPIFFE/SVIDs via Vault for mTLS
- OPA policies loaded via Docker Config
- Sigver sidecar for per-request validation
- Canary rollout with latency/error thresholds and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo example: verify image signature before starting app
async function verifySignature(image) {
  const sig = await notary.verify(image);
  if (!sig || !sig.valid) throw new Error('invalid image');
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle signature revocation and key rotation in this setup?
- How would you scale the sigver and policy sidecars across nodes?
